+# Compatibility research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1 – Path For Dell VxRail Customers** — VMware Cloud Foundation Product Management, Broadcom. https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2026/06/16/vmware-cloud-foundation-9-1-path-for-dell-vxrail-customers/
+  The supported in-place path requires VCF 5.2.2 or later and VxRail 8.0.361 or later, but stretched clusters, dynamic nodes, two-node clusters, and satellite nodes have to wait for a release after 9.1. That boundary makes an in-place 9.1 upgrade invalid for the fixture even though its component versions meet the general minimums; the design therefore uses a greenfield replacement.
+
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, article 440630. https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  VCF 9.1 requires VCF Management Services and a centralized license server. Management Services needs at least 12 management-network IPs and can grow to 30; its default internal range is 198.18.0.0/15. The same article records that VCF Operations precedes the platform lifecycle flow and that legacy Aria Log Insight data moves into VCF Log Management before the old appliance is decommissioned.
+
+- **Support and upgrade requirements for NSX 9.x in VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) 9.x** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, article 401775. https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/401775/nsx-9x-is-only-supported-as-part-of-a-vc.html
+  NSX 4.x to 9.x is supported only through VCF lifecycle tooling. The migration plan consequently gates the NSX target on VCF lifecycle and does not describe an independent NSX upgrade.
+
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation – Upgrade Bundle Details** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, article 327207. https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/327207/vmware-cloud-foundation-upgrade-bundle.html
+  The VCF 5.2.2 bundle inventory corroborates the fixture's SDDC Manager, vCenter, ESXi, and NSX source builds. This establishes that the fixture is internally coherent before applying its separate VxRail-topology boundary.
+
+- **Could not retrieve binary for component during “Deploy and Validate” in VCF 9.1** — Broadcom Knowledge Base, article 436258. https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/436258/could-not-retrieve-binary-for-component.html
+  The article identifies the active 9.1.0.0 BOM examples for SDDC Manager, vCenter, and NSX and warns that a deployment JSON must match the depot BOM. The artifact uses the seed's pinned 9.1.0.0 builds rather than newer live patch levels.
+
+- **vmware/vcf-api-specs, tag 9.1.0.0** — VMware by Broadcom on GitHub. https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/tree/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer
+  The repository supplies the Apache-2.0 VCF Installer OpenAPI document used to validate `greenfield.sddcSpec`; the vendored file is the tag's `specifications/vcf-installer/vcf-installer-openapi.json`.
